  "reason": "With no prior experiments, there is no evidence to guide exploitation, so the priority is establishing a clean, minimal baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the design space: a single RNA profile encoded with PCA (2000 dims), no aggregation, no image modality, no fusion. This minimizes implementation risk and confounding factors. It directly enables the next set of high-value comparisons: (a) does multiprofile + aggregation help? (compare to config_002/003), (b) do learned RNA encoders (scVI, scGPT) improve over PCA? (compare to config_004/007), and (c) does adding an image modality via concat fusion help? (compare to config_016). Without this reference, we cannot attribute performance gains to any specific design choice. Starting with the simplest modality and encoder is the most information-efficient first experiment under a limited budget."
}

